From 59cf9eb3bdfdc2ed727c8cf35c418f4a56de0391 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Max Horn <max@quendi.de>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:09:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] julia-gc: Count young bags marked by another thread

`MarkBag` counted a young, unmarked bag as a young reference only if
`jl_gc_mark_queue_obj` returned 1. Up to Julia 1.9 that return value
told whether the object is young. Since Julia 1.10
(JuliaLang/julia#47292) it tells whether the call set the mark bit,
and with several GC threads another thread can set it first.

The reference then went uncounted, the old bag holding it was not put
into the remembered set, and the next quick collection freed the young
bag while the old one still referenced it.

Count the reference whenever the GC bits say that the bag is young.

Assisted-by: Claude Code (Opus 5.5)
---
 src/julia_gc.c | 15 ++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/julia_gc.c b/src/julia_gc.c
index ee9e1ed55..c6a39bfb8 100644
--- a/src/julia_gc.c
+++ b/src/julia_gc.c
@@ -1048,16 +1048,17 @@ inline void MarkBag(Bag bag, void * ref)
 #endif
     }
 #endif
-    // The following code is a performance optimization and
-    // relies on Julia internals. It is functionally equivalent
-    // to:
-    //
-    //     if (JMarkTyped(p, DatatypeGapObj)) ((MarkData *)ref)->youngRef++;
-    //
+    // Mark `p` and count it if it is young: an old bag referencing a young
+    // one has to stay in the remembered set. The GC bits tell whether `p`
+    // is young, which relies on Julia internals. The return value of
+    // jl_gc_mark_queue_obj does not tell: it is 0 for a young bag that
+    // another GC thread marked first.
     switch (jl_astaggedvalue(p)->bits.gc) {
     case 0:
-        if (JMarkTyped(((MarkData *)ref)->ptls, p, DatatypeGapObj))
+        if (jl_typeis(p, DatatypeGapObj)) {
+            jl_gc_mark_queue_obj(((MarkData *)ref)->ptls, p);
             ((MarkData *)ref)->youngRef++;
+        }
         break;
     case 1:
         ((MarkData *)ref)->youngRef++;
